# Git Commit Rules

## Never run git commit
Never run `git commit` yourself. Ever. Not even with --amend.

## Workflow
1. Stage files when the user says to stage
2. After staging, propose a commit message
3. Stop. The user runs the commit themselves.
4. After the user says "pushed", read and follow the `update-pr` skill to offer creating or updating the PR.

## Commit message style
- Concise, factual, imperative mood
- No filler phrases — say what changed
- No trailing period

## Never suggest or add
- `Co-authored-by` trailers of any kind
- `--author` flags referencing AI tools
